<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kyi, Shchek and Khoryv</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kyi, Kyi, Shchek and Khoriv</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kyi, Shchek and Khoryv are three legendary brothers who, with their sister Lybid, are credited in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/primary-chronicle">Primary Chronicle</a> with founding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kiev</a> on the hills above the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dnieper">Dnieper</a>. Kyi, the eldest, gave the city its name, and the chronicle names hills and the Lybid river after the others. The legend reflects the early history of the Polans, the East Slavic tribe of the Kiev region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kyi-shchek-and-khoryv.jpg" alt="Kyi, Shchek and Khoryv" width="320" height="247" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kyi,_Czech,_Khoryv_and_Lubed_in_der_Radziwi%C5%82%C5%82chronik.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
